 4. ICYMI: Bark or bite 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Colossal Biosciences CEO Ben Lamm and Anduril Industries founder Palmer Luckey have a new gig: Warhound, valued at $1.2 billion.

 Why it matters: We're talking genetically modified and cybernetic-enhanced military working dogs here.

 Catch up quick: My colleagues Lucinda Shen and Dan Primack covered this late last week.

 Take No. 1, here . Take No. 2, here . My thought bubble: There was once a time when defense and national security were dirty words. Then it became OK to invest in weapons — but only the defensive ones. Now, people are advertising anything-as-a-service .

 Will man's best friend be a step too far? What's next: Lamm joins us Nov. 19 onstage at the Future of Defense Summit. Request an invite to attend ASAP !

 
 
