 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 An F-35 cuts across the sky at Nellis Air Force Base, Nevada. Photo: Colin Demarest/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 📈 The Pentagon and Lockheed Martin struck a deal funding a decade of F-35 production and upkeep, with the world's largest defense contractor by revenue covering some $7 billion in supporting "initiatives."

 Why it matters: It's a massive, massive commitment. (Do you know what you'll be up to in two years, let alone 10?) 💭 My thought bubble: Neither the Defense Department nor Lockheed laid out a "total value or per-jet price," as Defense News noted. 💥 Denmark is buying Kongsberg's Joint Strike Missile and Covenant's Anthem, a much newer munition the startup has described as a Tomahawk alternative.

 Why it matters: "The acquisitions are a significant step toward making Denmark better able to defend itself, strengthening NATO and increasing our ability to strike back," Danish Defense Minister ​Jeppe Bruus said in a translated statement. 💭 My thought bubble: This is a big win for Covenant, which emerged from stealth in September. 🤖 Applied Intuition is furnishing for the U.S. Navy its Data Engine and Intelligent Perception System, which together collate data from disparate sensors and lay out information for users. The multimillion-dollar deal begins with five Arleigh Burke-class destroyers.

 Why it matters: "Today's surface warfare picture depends on brittle manual processes, and data is siloed across networks and paper logs," co-founder Peter Ludwig said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: Applied was valued at $15 billion last summer. 🔋 Radiant will deploy its Kaleidos microreactor at Naval Weapons Station Crane in Indiana, in conjunction with its Janus work for the U.S. Army. Final environmental reviews, local site design and more are to come.

 Why it matters: The Pentagon is "actively breaking down the barriers that have prevented deployment of nuclear reactors," Mike Dodd, assistant secretary of defense for critical tech, said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: My colleague Esteban Hernandez wrote about Radiant's plans for Buckley Space Force Base, Colorado, earlier this year. Give it a read ! 
 
